      "Rx(90°)Ry(90°) =  matrix([0,0,1],[1,0,0],[0,1,0])\nRy(90°)Rx(90°) =  matrix([0,1,0],[0,0,-1],[-1,0,0])\nthey differ:      matrix([0,-1,1],[1,0,1],[1,1,0])\naxis/angle of the first :\n                          [[0.5773502691896258,0.5773502691896258,\n                            0.5773502691896258],2.0943951023931953]\naxis/angle of the second:\n                          [[0.5773502691896258,0.5773502691896258,\n                            -0.5773502691896258],2.0943951023931953]\ngeneric Euler matrix, entry (3,1) =  -sin(theta)   (= −sin θ)\nat θ = π/2:\nmatrix([0,sin(psi-phi),cos(psi-phi)],[0,cos(psi-phi),-sin(psi-phi)],[-1,0,0])\nsame matrix with φ → φ+c, ψ → ψ+c  (c arbitrary):\ndifference =  matrix([0,0,0],[0,0,0],[0,0,0])\n— one whole degree of freedom has vanished: gimbal lock"
     ]
    }
   ]
