   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "source": "## References\n\n- ★ Lee, N.-H. (2020) *Geometry: from Isometries to Special Relativity*. Cham: Springer. doi:10.1007/978-3-030-42101-4. Chapter 3 for rotations of the sphere and the orthogonal group.\n- Altmann, S.L. (1986) *Rotations, Quaternions, and Double Groups*. Oxford: Clarendon Press. The definitive careful treatment of the double cover and of the sign conventions that trip people up.\n- Stillwell, J. (2008) *Naive Lie Theory*. New York: Springer. Chapters 1–3 develop $SO(3)$, $SU(2)$ and the covering map at exactly the level used here.\n\nEuler's rotation theorem appears in *Formulae generales pro translatione quacunque corporum rigidorum*, presented to the St Petersburg Academy in 1775 and published in *Novi Commentarii academiae scientiarum Petropolitanae* 20 (1776) — both dates are cited in the literature, which is why none is given in the statement above.\n\nRodrigues' formula is due to Olinde Rodrigues (1840). Hamilton's quaternions date from 1843.\n---\n*Marked ★ = in the local indexed library (`maths` collection); the rest are standard references given from knowledge, not consulted here. Every code cell in this notebook was executed and its output is the real result; the prose is written from knowledge and checked against these sources where they cover the material.*",
